-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0 12px;font-size:.9rem"><strong>Adult notes — access &amp; sensory</strong><br>Bodies and food are personal. Teach every idea on the model, the diagram or the picture card — never on a pupil's own body, and never on what a pupil has eaten. If a pupil steps out, the diagram waits for them.</div><div class="scaffold-print-box"><h3>Sentence stems</h3><p>I will show you my proof out loud so you can copy the shape: 'The robin is a vertebrate BECAUSE I can see the line of small bones down its back.' Because. That word is where the evidence goes.</p><h3>Word bank</h3><p>backbone, vertebrate, invertebrate, skeleton, support</p></div></div><div id="print-scaffold-standard" class="print-section"><h2>Scaffolding — ▲ Standard</h2><div class="scaffold-print-box"><h3>Sentence stems</h3><p>I will show you my proof out loud so you can copy the shape: 'The robin is a vertebrate BECAUSE I can see the line of small bones down its back.' Because. That word is where the evidence goes.</p><h3>Word bank</h3><p>backbone, vertebrate, invertebrate, skeleton, support</p></div></div><div id="print-scaffold-stretch" class="print-section"><h2>Scaffolding — ★ Stretch</h2><div class="scaffold-print-box"><h3>Sentence stems</h3><p>I will show you my proof out loud so you can copy the shape: 'The robin is a vertebrate BECAUSE I can see the line of small bones down its back.' Because. That word is where the evidence goes.</p><h3>Word bank</h3><p>backbone, vertebrate, invertebrate, skeleton, support</p></div></div><div id="print-worksheet-supported" class="print-section"><h2>Independent Work — ◆ Supported</h2><div class="prevent-break"><p><strong>Task:</strong> Cut and stick eight animal cards onto the two-column mat. Word bank on the sheet.</p><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div></div></div><div id="print-worksheet-stan