h surface three times. Carpet gave the shortest distance every time, so carpet produced the most friction.</p></div><div id="print-scaffold-supported" class="print-section"><h2>Scaffolding — ◆ Supported</h2><div style="border:1px solid #999;border-left:6px solid #3F7D6E;background:#3F7D6E14;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;margin:8px 0 12px;font-size:.9rem"><strong>Adult notes — access &amp; sensory</strong><br>Forces work is noisy and physical — trolleys, ramps, dropped masses. Agree the noise signal before equipment comes out, and offer ear defenders without making it a conversation. A pupil may record data instead of running the trial and still be doing the science.</div><div class="scaffold-print-box"><h3>Sentence stems</h3><p>Write it as one planning sentence before you touch equipment: 'I will change ____, keep ____ and ____ the same, and measure ____ in ____.' If you cannot finish that sentence, you are not ready to test.</p><h3>Word bank</h3><p>variable, independent variable, control variable, dependent variable, repeat</p></div></div><div id="print-scaffold-standard" class="print-section"><h2>Scaffolding — ▲ Standard</h2><div class="scaffold-print-box"><h3>Sentence stems</h3><p>Write it as one planning sentence before you touch equipment: 'I will change ____, keep ____ and ____ the same, and measure ____ in ____.' If you cannot finish that sentence, you are not ready to test.</p><h3>Word bank</h3><p>variable, independent variable, control variable, dependent variable, repeat</p></div></div><div id="print-scaffold-stretch" class="print-section"><h2>Scaffolding — ★ Stretch</h2><div class="scaffold-print-box"><h3>Sentence stems</h3><p>Write it as one planning sentence before you touch equipment: 'I will change ____, keep ____ and ____ the same, and measure ____ in ____.' If you cannot finish that sentence, you are not ready to test.</p><h3>Word bank</h3><p>variable, independent variable, control variable, dependent variable, repeat</p></div></div><div id="print-worksheet-supported" class="print-section"><h2>Independent Work — ◆ Supported</h2><div class="prevent-break"><p><strong>Task:</strong> Complete the planning frame from the word bank, then run three trials and fill the table.</p><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div></div></div><div id="print-worksheet-standard" class="print-section"><h2>Independent Work — ▲ Standard</h2><div class="prevent-break"><p><strong>Task:</strong> Write your own planning frame, run three trials per surface, and complete the table with units.</p><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div></div></div><div id="print-worksheet-stretch" class="print-section"><h2>Independent Work — ★ Stretch</h2><div class="prevent-break"><p><strong>Task:</strong> Plan, run three trials per surface, calculate the mean, and write a conclusion that states whether the data answers the question.</p><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div></div></div><div id="print-exit" class="print-section"><h2>Exit Ticket</h2><p>Name one control variable from today's test.</p><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div></div><div id="print-witness" class="print-section"><h1 style="text-align:center;font-size:1.5rem;margin-bottom:2px">Assessor Witness Statement</h1><p style="text-align:center;margin:0 0 10px;font-size:.88rem"><strong>Pearson Entry Level Science 8939 (E1→E3); AQA UAS science units</strong><br>AQA UAS unit code: TBC (Cheryl). Records what was observed, and at which level of independence.</p><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.93rem;margin-bottom:10px"><tr><td style="padding:7px 8px;border:1px solid #999;width:34%"><strong>Pupil</strong></td><td style="padding:7px 8px;border:1px solid #999">____________________</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:7px 8px;border:1px solid #999;width:34%"><strong>Lesson</strong></td><td style="padding:7px 8px;border:1px solid #999">Planning a Fair Test — GROW Science · Week 5</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:7px 8px;border:1px solid #999;width:34%"><strong>Date</strong></td><td style="padding:7px 8px;border:1px solid #999">____________________</td></tr></table><p style="margin:12px 0 4px;font-weight:800;font-size:.95rem">Observed in this lesson</p><p style="margin:0 0 5px">☐ Identified independent, dependent and control variables.</p><p style="margin:0 0 5px">☐ Recorded results in a table with correct units.</p><p style="margin:0 0 5px">☐ Judged whether the data answered the question.</p><p style="margin:12px 0 4px;font-weight:800;font-size:.95rem">Assessor comment</p><div style="border:1px solid #999;height:26px;margin-bottom:5px"></div><div style="border:1px solid #999;height:26px;margin-bottom:5px"></div><p style="margin:12px 0 4px;font-weight:800;font-size:.95rem">Ring the tier the pupil actually worked at</p><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.88rem"><tr><td style="padding:9px;border:2px solid #333;width:33.3%;text-align:center"><strong>◆ Supported</strong></td><td style="padding:9px;border:2px solid #333;width:33.3%;text-align:center"><strong>▲ Standard</strong></td><td style="padding:9px;border:2px solid #333;width:33.3%;text-align:center"><strong>★ Stretch</strong></td></tr></table><p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:.82rem">Assessor name ______________ Role ____________ Signature ______________ Date ________</p></div><div id="print-lundy" class="print-section"><h2>Lundy Loop</h2><p><strong>Space:</strong> This lesson has a lot of waiting between trials. Waiting is part of it, not wasted time.</p><p><strong>Voice:</strong> Tell me if you think my method is flawed. You will sometimes be right.</p><p><strong>Audience:</strong> Your planning frame and table go into the Entry Level Science evidence folder.</p><p><strong>Influence:</strong> The class agrees the one variable the whole group investigates next.</p><p style="font-size:.95rem;margin:.5rem 0 0"><strong>Closing the loop:</strong> this one ends on paper &mdash; your own hand, or your words scribed by an adult. Saying it aloud starts the loop; writing it is what closes it. Pass is always allowed.</p><p style="font-size:.9rem;color:#444;margin:.4rem 0 .2rem">What I said, and what it changed:</p><div class="print-line"></div><div class="print-line"></div></div><div id="print-feedback" class="print-section"><h2 style="text-align:center">Planning a Fair Test — Feedback Sheet</h2><p style="font-size:.95rem;color:#444">Keep with your portfolio.</p><table class="ko-table"><tr><td style="width:50%"><strong>Pupil name:</strong></td><td><strong>Date:</strong></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2"><strong>WWW (What Went Well):</strong><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div></td></tr><tr><td colspan="2"><strong>EBI (Even Better If):</strong><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Level worked at:</strong> Supported / Standard / Stretch</td><td><strong>Evidence filed:</strong> Yes / Not yet</td></tr><tr><td colspan="2"><strong>Pupil response — my next step:</strong><div class='print-line'></div></td></tr></table></div></div><script>
